note SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
note Select CPU (0) or GB10 (1) for a single sparse hop. Compose after
note om/runtime/rx_capq_core.om. The authority owns receipt authentication
note and qualification. Pass only observations it verified for this request.
note Key words: SHA-256 of workload, software identities, machine and math
note contract (four words), followed by nodes, arcs, batch and model variant.
note Rows append backend (0/1), count of paired measurements, end-to-end
note median nanoseconds and median microjoules. Zero metrics mean unavailable.
note Strictly lower latency plus non-increasing energy qualifies the GPU.
fn ar_observed key view ulong 8 row view ulong 12 backend ulong to bool
  for i ulong 8
    if ne get row i get key i
      ret false
    end
  end
  if ne get row 8 backend
    ret false
  end
  ret and ne get row 9 0 and ne get row 10 0 ne get row 11 0
end

fn arboris_capq key view ulong 8 cpu view ulong 12 gpu view ulong 12 to ulong
  if eq or get key 0 or get key 1 or get key 2 get key 3 0
    ret 0
  end
  if or eq get key 4 0 or eq get key 6 0 gt get key 7 1
    ret 0
  end
  if or not ar_observed key cpu 0 not ar_observed key gpu 1
    ret 0
  end
  if or ne get cpu 9 get gpu 9 ge get gpu 10 get cpu 10
    ret 0
  end
  a = new ulong 7 0
  b = new ulong 7 0
  dims = new uchar 7 0
  put dims 1 1
  for i ulong 2
    put a i get gpu add i 10
    put b i get cpu add i 10
  end
  ret rx_cq_dominates a b dims 2
end
